    "name":  "Hodgkin lymphoma",
    "module":  "oncology",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Hodgkin lymphoma (HL) is a malignancy of the lymphatic system arising from abnormal B-lymphocytes (Reed-Sternberg cells). It characteristically presents with painless lymphadenopathy, most commonly in the cervical or mediastinal regions. Constitutional B-symptoms (fever, drenching night sweats, \u003e10% weight loss in 6 months) occur in about 40% of patients and indicate more advanced or aggressive disease. HL is one of the most curable cancers with chemotherapy and/or radiotherapy, with 5-year survival exceeding 85% overall.",
